error[E0415]: no method `close` on `Receiver<i64>`
  --> tests/programs/concurrency/channels/e0415.la:3:8
  |
3 |     rx.close();
  |        ^^^^^
  |
  = help: only a `Sender` can `close`; this is the `Receiver` end

error[E0415]: `Chan` has no `buffered`
  --> tests/programs/concurrency/channels/e0415.la:4:25
  |
4 |     let old = Chan<i64>.buffered(2);
  |                         ^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: make a channel with `Chan<T>.new(n)`, holding up to `n` values (0: each handed over directly), or `Chan<T>.unbounded()`

For more about E0415, run `lughac explain E0415`.
